userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: For a projectile launched and landing at the same height, range depends on initial speed squared and on sin(2θ), so range quadruples when speed doubles, is maximized at 45°, and is identical for complementary launch angles even though their peak heights differ.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Range = v₀²sin(2θ)/g packs two separate lessons: speed enters squared (so it dominates), while angle enters through sin(2θ), which peaks at 45° and returns the same value for θ and 90° − θ.
DEMO STEPS: 7 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
